1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,589
Teacher midterm practice, question 37.

2
00:00:04,209 --> 00:00:09,348
True or false: generally, weakly bonded solids have a low melting point,

3
00:00:09,348 --> 00:00:13,936
a low elastic modulus, and a high thermal expansion coefficient.

4
00:00:15,636 --> 00:00:17,670
Use the bonding energy curve.

5
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:20,551
A weak bond is a shallow well, so little energy

6
00:00:20,551 --> 00:00:23,488
separates the atoms: a low melting point.

7
00:00:24,108 --> 00:00:27,979
The force curve is flatter at the equilibrium spacing, so the

8
00:00:27,979 --> 00:00:31,910
force rises slowly with stretch: a low elastic modulus.

9
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:35,941
And a shallow well is more asymmetric, so the atoms move

10
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:39,636
further apart as they vibrate: high thermal expansion.

11
00:00:41,235 --> 00:00:44,039
All three trends follow, so the answer is A: true.

12
00:00:44,859 --> 00:00:47,969
A weak bond means high thermal expansion, not low.
